    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee0185a0_ebb25553",
        "filename": "radio/1.5/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-09T20:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this mean that for update values of all fields need to be sent down to the modem? That doesn\u0027t seem like a good design to me from client perspective.\n\nJust wanted to call this out, although this is probably ok if you don\u0027t have an easy alternative.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 326,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 327,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "309fdc263f0a834552ce263fdb087c04122cf9b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa48a4d3_75a5c63c",
        "filename": "radio/1.5/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-09T20:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? We try not to have any optional requests in hal. In any case currently we don\u0027t really have any VTS for indications.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "309fdc263f0a834552ce263fdb087c04122cf9b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f1b58a9_29f8e37c",
        "filename": "radio/1.5/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1407086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-09T22:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From my point of view, this is an optimization that modem can support to speed up the phonebook caching. But it should not be an essential command that all modem supplier must support.\nIf I recall correctly, the Android code can handle both cases (supported and not supported).",
      "parentUuid": "aa48a4d3_75a5c63c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "309fdc263f0a834552ce263fdb087c04122cf9b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0897047_c501954d",
        "filename": "radio/1.5/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-09T22:12:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But getPhonebookRecords can only be called after this, so if it is not supported we will never know if getPhonebookRecords can be called or not. I think this should always be sent, and in case it is not supported the indication should have a parameter to convey that.",
      "parentUuid": "9f1b58a9_29f8e37c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "309fdc263f0a834552ce263fdb087c04122cf9b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e70bd0d0_4d789d62",
        "filename": "radio/1.5/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1407086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-09T22:23:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The proposal was to use a resource that indicates the support.\nSee https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1156377.",
      "parentUuid": "f0897047_c501954d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "309fdc263f0a834552ce263fdb087c04122cf9b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
